//! The `overflow-anchor` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property provides a
//! way to opt out of the browser's scroll anchoring behavior, which adjusts scroll position to
//! minimize content shifts.
//!
//! Initial: auto. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - auto: The element becomes a potential anchor when adjusting scroll position.
//! - none: The element won't be selected as a potential anchor.
//!
//! Grammar: auto | none
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-scroll-anchoring-1/#propdef-overflow-anchor
//!
//! Author guide:
